  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules weaken S2 and S5: the 5% thermal-test failure rate is only a review trigger with no automatic sales ban, and the 8/100k recall trigger leads to regulator review with recall only if the regulator finds risk cannot be mitigated. S1 requires confirmed incidents only, with 24-hour initial reporting and 5-business-day customer notice. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 72-month retrofit deadline; S4 requires built-in or validated equivalent suppression from 36 months."
